### ============================================================================
### Workflow HITL Sample - Content Moderation with Human Approval
### ============================================================================
### This sample demonstrates MAF workflows with human-in-the-loop using the
### request_info / @response_handler pattern on Azure Durable Functions.
###
### The AgentFunctionApp automatically provides all HITL endpoints.
###
### Prerequisites:
### 1. Start Azurite: azurite --silent --location .
### 2. Start Durable Task Scheduler emulator
### 3. Configure local.settings.json with Azure OpenAI credentials
### 4. Run: func start
### ============================================================================


### Start the full workflow.
### This route now runs a custom executor pipeline:
### input_router -> drafter -> editor (HITL pause) -> finalizer

POST http://localhost:7071/api/workflow/run
Content-Type: application/json

"Write a brief introduction to artificial intelligence."

### You can also send a structured JSON body; the input router will convert it to a prompt.

POST http://localhost:7071/api/workflow/run
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Introduction to artificial intelligence",
  "body": "Artificial intelligence helps systems reason over data, automate repetitive work, and support human decision-making.",
}

### ============================================================================


@instanceId = 28b43898e9614cab85205e25e98a992f

GET http://localhost:7071/api/workflow/status/{{instanceId}}

### ============================================================================


@requestId = cf83544a-2f26-4777-9b2a-de8fd6d551d6

POST http://localhost:7071/api/workflow/respond/{{instanceId}}/{{requestId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "approved": true,
  "feedback": "Looks good."
}


### ============================================================================
### 5. Reject And Ask For Another Editor Pass
### ============================================================================
### This keeps the workflow paused on editor until the revision is acceptable.

POST http://localhost:7071/api/workflow/respond/{{instanceId}}/{{requestId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "approved": false,
  "feedback": "Please make the draft shorter and more executive in tone."
}


### ============================================================================
### Health Check
### ============================================================================

GET http://localhost:7071/api/health